An opt-in `--release-verified-modules` option of `dafny verify` drops the bodies of a module's methods, lemmas, constructors and iterators once the module is verified and reported, so that memory stays near what one module needs beyond the resolved program. The output is unchanged; a later read of a dropped body throws an exception. The translator now tests whether a member of another module is in the verification scope before it reads that member's body.
